0 @WEB_C_penhallow@ _CHAP
1 REFN penhallow
1 TITL From St Just to Shake Rag Street
1 _SUBTITLE Penhallow & Trembath
1 _ORDER 1
1 _SECTION wedding
2 TITL A wedding at Penzance
2 _ORDER 1
2 DATE 1866
2 _PERIOD 1866–1868
2 NOTE John Penhallow, a tin miner from St Just, married Elizabeth Ann Trembath at the Wesleyan Methodist Chapel in Penzance on 9 October 1866. He was twenty-one and she was nineteen. John signed his name, and Elizabeth made her mark.
2 NOTE Their son Richard was born at Penzance the next September. In the spring of 1868 the three of them sailed from Liverpool. They arrived in New York on 14 May, bound for Wisconsin.
2 _PERSON @I0001@
2 _PERSON @I0002@
