3 _HASH 193d14f541e7f47f53ba17dd3389261c29effe0095d3de641d13e01dc43cc98a
1 _SECTION mineral-point
2 TITL Forty years in Mineral Point
2 _ORDER 2
2 DATE 1868
2 _PERIOD 1868–1923
2 NOTE The family reached Mineral Point in June 1868, and baby Richard died there that year. In 1880 John was working as a miner. Elizabeth kept house, with Mary Jane, nine, and William Henry, two.
2 NOTE For more than thirty years John worked in the lead and zinc mines around the town, and later at the zinc works. He was a class leader in the Methodist church. He died at his home on Shake Rag Street on 3 March 1912. Elizabeth died in Mineral Point in January 1923.
2 _PERSON @I0001@
